==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 30~40 seconds<sup>900f~1,200f</sup>.
*5 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns after 36 seconds<sup>1,080f</sup>.
*1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Satanmaria (Enemy)|Satanmaria]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Zir Zeal]]s spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
**4 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**1 [[Super Devil (Enemy)|Super Devil]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Despite the low magnification peons, Satanmaria works synergistically with Zir Zeal and Zory's burrow, usually letting the bosses push all the way to your base. Because of this, you'll want to cover your tracks with a consistent line of [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cats]] at all time. Do your best to wait out all three Zackie Pengs, since it makes handling everything later on a whole lot easier.

Your win condition is to outlast both of the Zir Zeals, letting you target Satanmaria with your King Dragon Cats directly. The various Zoges and Zrocos make this somewhat difficult, though, so bring [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] for extra damage on unburrowing Zombies.

